"type":3,"x":65,"y":26},{"type":3,"x":66,"y":26},{"type":2,"x":61,"y":27},{"type":2,"x":70,"y":36},{"type":2,"x":51,"y":37}],"enemies":[{"type":"bat","x":60,"y":7},{"type":"bat","x":14,"y":10},{"type":"bat","x":42,"y":10},{"type":"bat","x":62,"y":11},{"type":"snake","x":5,"y":18},{"type":"crab","x":22,"y":21},{"type":"snake","x":5,"y":26},{"type":"spider","x":26,"y":30},{"type":"spider","x":52,"y":30}],"pads":[],"triviaQuestion":"","triviaAnswer":"","triviaTrap":"","triviaPos":null,"gates":[{"question":"Which element sits directly below carbon in the table?","answer":"Si","pos":{"x":26,"y":11},"pads":[{"x":26,"y":10,"key":"Ge"},{"x":28,"y":10,"key":"Si"},{"x":30,"y":10,"key":"N"}],"doors":[{"x":18,"y":13},{"x":34,"y":13},{"x":12,"y":24}]},{"question":"Which noble gas ends period 3, the row that starts with sodium?","answer":"Ar","pos":{"x":57,"y":4},"pads":[{"x":57,"y":3,"key":"Ar"},{"x":59,"y":3,"key":"Kr"},{"x":61,"y":3,"key":"Ne"}],"doors":[{"x":69,"y":2},{"x":69,"y":26}]},{"question":"The lanthanides fill a gap in period 6. Which element comes just before the gap?","answer":"Ba","pos":{"x":14,"y":28},"pads":[{"x":14,"y":27,"key":"Hf"},{"x":16,"y":27,"key":"Cs"},{"x":18,"y":27,"key":"Ba"}],"doors":[{"x":12,"y":29}]},{"question":"Uranium is element 92. Which element comes straight after it?","answer":"Np","pos":{"x":5,"y":38},"pads":[{"x":5,"y":37,"key":"Pu"},{"x":7,"y":37,"key":"Np"},{"x":9,"y":37,"key":"Pa"}],"doors":[{"x":4,"y":36}]}],"families":[{"name":"Group 1","keys":["H","Li","Na","K","Rb","Cs","Fr"],"bonus":50,"color":"#ff7b7b"},{"name":"Group 2","keys":["Be","Mg","Ca","Sr","Ba","Ra"],"bonus":55,"color":"#ffb35c"},{"name":"Groups 3–12 · period 4","keys":["Sc","Ti","V","Cr","Mn","Fe","Co","Ni","Cu","Zn"],"bonus":130,"color":"#f2d14e"},{"name":"Groups 3–12 · period 5","keys":["Y","Zr","Nb","Mo","Tc","Ru","Rh","Pd","Ag","Cd"],"bonus":40,"color":"#d9c2a0"},{"name":"Groups 4–12 · period 6","keys":["Hf","Ta","W","Re","Os","Ir","Pt","Au","Hg"],"bonus":40,"color":"#c9a36b"},{"name":"Group 13","keys":["B","Al","Ga","In","Tl"],"bonus":30,"color":"#9be07b"},{"name":"Group 14","keys":["C","Si","Ge","Sn","Pb"],"bonus":25,"color":"#5ad1a0"},{"name":"Group 15","keys":["N","P","As","Sb","Bi"],"bonus":15,"color":"#5ad1c8"},{"name":"Group 16","keys":["O","S","Se","Te","Po"],"bonus":15,"color":"#6ec6ff"},{"name":"Group 17","keys":["F","Cl","Br","I","At"],"bonus":30,"color":"#8f9bff"},{"name":"Group 18","keys":["He","Ne","Ar","Kr","Xe","Rn"],"bonus":45,"color":"#c792ea"},{"name":"Lanthanides","keys":["La","Ce","Pr","Nd","Pm","Sm","Eu","Gd","Tb","Dy","Ho","Er","Tm","Yb","Lu"],"bonus":45,"color":"#ff8fb1"},{"name":"Actinides · Ac to Pu","keys":["Ac","Th","Pa","U","Np","Pu"],"bonus":30,"color":"#b0b7c3"}],"hints":[{"x":28,"y":3,"r":2,"icon":"🗺️","title":"THE TABLE RUN","text":"This mine is dug in the shape of the <strong>periodic table</strong>. Every element lies where it sits in the table: hydrogen far to the west, helium far to the east, the transition metals below you. A row of the table is a <strong>period</strong>, a column is a <strong>group</strong>. Go where you like - finish a group and <strong>time goes back on the clock</strong>."},{"x":28,"y":9,"r":1,"icon":"🚪","title":"THE DOORS ASK ABOUT THE TABLE","text":"The doors below lead down to the <strong>transition metals</strong>, the ten columns in the middle of the table. Every question in this mine is about where an element sits - so look at the table as you dig."},{"x":6,"y":12,"r":2,"icon":"🌊","title":"THE FIRST TWO COLUMNS","text":"The alkali metals and the alkaline earth metals. From potassium down this shaft is flooded: swim down and leave by the tunnel at the bottom. (In a real laboratory the alkali metals are kept well away from water - they react with it, some of them violently.)"},{"x":18,"y":14,"r":1,"icon":"🛒","title":"ORE CARTS","text":"The carts on this track never stop. Wait in a side pocket until one has passed, then run for the next pocket."},{"x":27,"y":17,"r":2,"icon":"🔐","title":"THE STRONGROOM","text":"Ruthenium, rhodium, palladium and silver above; osmium, iridium, platinum and gold below. The <strong>precious metals</strong> are kept behind locked doors. A key lies in the gap at the west end of the row below."},{"x":12,"y":22,"r":1,"icon":"🕳️","title":"THE GAP IN PERIOD 6","text":"Between barium and hafnium, <strong>fifteen elements</strong> belong here: the lanthanides. They are drawn in a row of their own below the table so that it does not grow too wide. This shaft leads down to them."},{"x":55,"y":6,"r":2,"icon":"🪜","title":"THE STAIRCASE","text":"East of here the nonmetals lie in open air; below and west, the metals lie in the earth. The <strong>ice tunnel</strong> between them follows the stepped line that divides the two. The elements along it - boron, silicon, germanium, arsenic, antimony, tellurium - are the <strong>metalloids</strong>."},{"x":64,"y":7,"r":1,"icon":"☁️","title":"THE HALOGENS","text":"Fluorine and chlorine are <strong>poisonous gases</strong>, and the halogen shaft is full of gas. Take the gas mask, press <strong>4</strong> and move quickly: it lasts 20 seconds. The shaft opens at the bottom into row 7."},{"x":66,"y":26,"r":1,"icon":"☁️","title":"THE HALOGENS, FROM BELOW","text":"The shaft above you holds the halogens, astatine to fluorine, and it is full of gas. Take the gas mask, press <strong>4</strong> and climb quickly: it lasts 20 seconds. A tunnel at the top leads out beside oxygen."},{"x":62,"y":2,"r":2,"icon":"👑","title":"THE LAST COLUMN","text":"The <strong>noble gases</strong> fill the last column of the table, helium at the top. They react with almost nothing - so nothing guards them but this door."},{"x":13,"y":26,"r":1,"icon":"🔬","title":"ROW SEVEN","text":"The superheavy elements of period 7 were made in laboratories, a few atoms at a time. They are buried in this seam: take a Geiger counter, press <strong>3</strong> and dig along the row. Pure bonus."},{"x":12,"y":30,"r":1,"icon":"🚧","title":"THE TUNNEL BORER","text":"A borer runs back and forth under the lanthanides. It cuts through anything and never stops. Use its tunnel as a road - and climb out of it when the machine comes."},{"x":9,"y":36,"r":2,"icon":"☢️","title":"THE ACTINIDES","text":"Every actinide is <strong>radioactive</strong>. Actinium to plutonium lie along this row, over pits of lava - do not step down. East of plutonium the elements were made in reactors and laboratories; they are buried, and need the Geiger counter."}]}